### Please describe the problem in your own words.

In a `sizebalanced` group, `git annex sync --content --rebalance` does not
stop at an even split. It keeps moving files off the fullest repository
until that repository is almost empty, and the next run moves nearly
everything back.


### What steps will reproduce the problem?

Two repos in group `bal`, 20 files of 1 MB, all starting in `a`:

[[!format sh """
#!/bin/sh
set -e
git init -q a && cd a && git annex init -q a
for i in $(seq -w 1 20); do head -c 1000000 /dev/urandom > f$i; done
git annex add -q . && git commit -qm add
cd .. && git clone -q a b && (cd b && git annex init -q b)
cd a
git remote add b ../b
for r in here b; do
	git annex group $r bal
	git annex wanted $r groupwanted
	git annex maxsize $r 100MB
done
git annex groupwanted bal sizebalanced=bal
git annex sync --content --rebalance
echo "files in a: $(git annex find --in here | wc -l), in b: $(git annex find --in b | wc -l)"
"""]]

Output ends with `files in a: 0, in b: 20`. Expected about 10 in each.


### What version of git-annex are you using? On what operating system?

git-annex 10.20261020 (Arch Linux package 10.20261020-2), Linux 7.2.9.

